  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- Listener describes the intro piece as an awesome start to the performance [6]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Intro/Poem**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [8]\n- **Xmas Curtain**: back after 30 archived shows (637 days) [8]\n- **Golden**: with Kathleen Edwards [8]\n- **Into The Woods**: rare: 12 archived performances [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2005-10-22.km140.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 18 songs; 102 min [1]\n- **mmj2005-10-22.mk21-v3.flac24**: source not stated; 17 songs; 102 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]. Said about its sound: Recording features very good sound quality with little degradation noted by listener [5]\n- **mmj2005-10-22.mk21-v3.flac16**: source not stated; 17 songs; 103 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [3]\n- **mmj2005-10-22.chicago_partial**: FM broadcast; 9 songs; 58 min [4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Guests: Kathleen Edwards [1]\n- Reviewer previously dismissed band but changed mind after catching last song at Lollapalooza [6]\n- Listener expresses desire to hear the Kathleen Edwards collaboration included in broadcast [7]\n- WXRT planned to broadcast part of the concert on their Sunday Night Concert Series [2]\n- WXRT scheduled to air portions of the show on their Sunday Night Concert Series [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2005-10-22.km140.flac16**: taped by Ed; transferred by Ed; source: Neumann AK40 > LC3 > KM100 > Bumblebee MiAGi-II Silver Cables > Optimod V3 > NJB3/44.1khz [1]\n- **mmj2005-10-22.mk21-v3.flac24**: taped by Brian Skalinder; transferred by Brian Skalinder; source: (24-bit) Schoeps MK21/KC5/CMC6 (NOS) > Lunatec V3 > MicroTrack 2496 [2]. Also: Recorded from center balcony clamp using Schoeps MK21 mics and Lunatec V3 recorder [2]\n- **mmj2005-10-22.mk21-v3.flac16**: taped by Brian Skalinder; transferred by Brian Skalinder; source: (16-bit) Schoeps MK21/KC5/CMC6 (NOS) > Lunatec V3 > MicroTrack 2496 [3]. Also: Captured at 24-bit/44.1kHz via Schoeps MK21 mics connected to Lunatec V3 unit; Edited using Cool Edit Pro 2.0 for dithering and fades, plus CD-Wave tracking [3]\n- **mmj2005-10-22.chicago_partial**: source: fm [4]",
